  "blurb": "Level 3 of 3 — the advanced tier, for Designated Safeguarding Leads and deputies. This course goes well beyond Level 2: the statutory framework, thresholds and the continuum of need, high-quality referrals to children's social care, managing allegations against staff under KCSIE Part 4 and the LADO process, low-level concerns, positions of trust and safer culture, lawful multi-agency information sharing, contextual safeguarding, and rigorous record-keeping and chronologies. It is deliberately demanding — around 20 lessons and roughly two hours, best taken over several sittings — assumes you have completed Levels 1 and 2, and carries a higher 85% pass mark.",
