      "t": "Medicines fall into two broad groups, and your rules differ for each. Prescription medicines are prescribed by a doctor, dentist, nurse or pharmacist prescriber for a named child. Over-the-counter (OTC) medicines, such as paracetamol or antihistamine, can be bought without a prescription - but in a childcare setting they still need the same care and written consent before you give them."
