      "k": "text",
      "t": "Every child with asthma should have a personal asthma action plan agreed with their parents and doctor or nurse. This tells you their usual triggers, which inhalers they take and when, how to spot when their asthma is getting worse, and exactly what to do in an attack. Keep a copy where staff can find it quickly and check it as part of your setting's medical and care records."
